# 🌍 Language Translation Tool

A multi-feature web app that translates text, files, voice recordings, and images between 100+ languages — built for the **CodeAlpha Artificial Intelligence Internship (Task 1)**.

🔗 **Live App:** https://codealphalanguagetranslationtool-4jz7jem9ywhxyjc9tjud2m.streamlit.app/

---

## ✨ Features

- **✍️ Text Translation**
  - Auto-detects the input language and displays it
  - Manual override dropdown if auto-detection is wrong (especially useful for short text)
  - Translate into **up to 4 target languages simultaneously**, shown side by side
  - Text-to-speech playback for each translated result

- **📄 File Upload Translation**
  - Upload a `.txt` file
  - Automatically chunks long text to stay within API limits
  - Download the translated file directly

- **🎤 Voice Input**
  - Record your voice live in the browser (mic access) **or** upload an audio file (WAV/AIFF/FLAC)
  - Converts speech to text, translates it, and plays back the translated audio

- **🖼️ Image Translation (OCR)**
  - Upload an image (sign, menu, document, screenshot)
  - Extracts text using Tesseract OCR
  - Auto-detects and corrects image orientation for better accuracy
  - Translates the extracted text

---

## 🛠️ Tech Stack

|         Purpose      |                                     Library                                     |
|-          -         -|-                                       -                                       -|
| Web app framework    | [Streamlit](https://streamlit.io)                                               |
| Translation          | [deep-translator](https://pypi.org/project/deep-translator/) (Google Translate) |
| Language detection   | [langdetect](https://pypi.org/project/langdetect/)                              |
| Text-to-speech       | [gTTS](https://pypi.org/project/gTTS/)                                          |
| Speech-to-text       | [SpeechRecognition](https://pypi.org/project/SpeechRecognition/)                |
| Live audio recording | [audio-recorder-streamlit](https://pypi.org/project/audio-recorder-streamlit/)  |
| OCR (image → text)   | [pytesseract](https://pypi.org/project/pytesseract/) + Tesseract OCR            |
| Image handling       | [Pillow](https://pypi.org/project/Pillow/)                                      |

---

## 🚀 Run Locally

```bash
# Clone the repo
git clone https://github.com/<your-username>/CodeAlpha_LanguageTranslationTool.git
cd CodeAlpha_LanguageTranslationTool

# Install dependencies
pip install -r requirements.txt

# Run the app
streamlit run app.py
```

The app will open automatically at `http://localhost:8501`.

> **Note:** OCR requires the Tesseract binary installed on your system.
> - Windows: [Tesseract installer](https://github.com/UB-Mannheim/tesseract/wiki)
> - Mac: `brew install tesseract`
> - Linux: `sudo apt install tesseract-ocr`

